-- a root (part of language-implementation-remainder; Avik, 2026-11-22: "There is no canonical state";
-- "They are literally different mathematical objects"): one hash naming everything this machine's
-- paths hold, an object of the pool like any other. `hyperactive root` writes this machine's root to
-- the pool, says its hash, and names it beside the pool, where a machine with no labels starts from;
-- `hyperactive take ROOT` makes this machine's paths hold what that root says. A session is given a
-- root and hands one back; nothing another session wrote changes what this one's paths hold
hy-root-line : List (List Word) → List Word
hy-root-line (cons l r) = l
hy-root-line nil = nil
